.TH CLOSE 2
.SH NAME
close \- close a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B close(fildes)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Given a file descriptor such as returned from an
.BR open ,
.BR creat ,
.BR dup ,
or
.BR pipe (2)
call,
.B close
closes the associated file.
A close of all files is
automatic on
.BR exit ,
but since there is a limit on the number of open files
per process,
.B close
is necessary for programs which deal with many files.
.PP
Files are closed upon termination of a process, and certain file descriptors
may be closed by
.BR exec (2)
(see
.BR ioctl (2)).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
creat(2), dup(2), open(2), pipe(2), exec(2), ioctl(2)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Zero is returned if a file is closed; \-1 is returned for an unknown file
descriptor.
.SH ASSEMBLER
(close = 6.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
R0 = fildes
sys close
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 6
AX = fildes
int 0Xf1
.fi
.sp
